The two track vehicle model
As mentioned before, the bicycle model is a good approach for studying the vehicle´s motion in steady state conditions. However, for this VDM additional DOF like the roll and pitch motions and the vertical dynamics need to be studied, and the bicycle model is not the most suitable solution. Since a more complex model is needed for this application, the logic solution is to develop a two track vehicle model, based on the existing theory, and include in it the features needed to obtain the necessary level of detail.
As established in the VDM characteristics, the six DOF of the vehicle cabin must be considered, so the vehicle movement in the plane, defined for the bicycle model, must be completed with the vehicle vertical displacement and the roll and pitch rotations.
